#TETHERVERSE FRONTEND — SHARED BUILD CONFIGURATION
#
# Committed on purpose. Next.js reads this file in every environment, so these
# are the defaults a build gets without anyone setting a dashboard variable
# first, which is the difference between a Worker that builds and one that
# stops with "missing build-time variable".
#
# ── What is allowed in here ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Nothing secret, and nothing that has to change without a rebuild. Only values
# that are already public and are needed when the bundle is compiled, because
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the client at build time - changing
# one means a new build and a new deploy, whoever sets it.
#
# ── What is deliberately not in here ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# TETHERVERSE_API_URL. The backend address is read at request time from the
# Worker's own configuration (wrangler.toml [vars], or a variable in the
# dashboard), so moving the API is an edit there and no rebuild at all. A copy
# in this file would be baked into the deployed Worker and would quietly take
# over whenever the Worker variable went missing.
#
# `next dev` and `next start` fall back to http://localhost:4000 on their own; a
# developer pointing at a remote API puts it in .env.local, which is ignored and
# outranks this file.

# ── Excel Play sign-in ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The accounts frontend that hosts the sign-in page. Browser-facing by design:
# the player is redirected here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXCEL_AUTH_FRONTEND_URL=https://auth.excelmec.org

# ── Launcher embed ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The origin allowed to frame the game and to deliver a bridged auth token. It
# becomes the CSP's frame-ancestors list, so it is an allowlist rather than a
# wildcard: every origin that embeds this app, and nothing else. Comma-separated
# for more than one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCHER_ORIGIN=https://play.excelmec.org
